---
/**
 * about.astro — About Us Page
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us — FreeFileTools"
  description="Learn about FreeFileTools, our mission to build fast, open-source, client-side web tools, and our commitment to absolute data privacy."
>
  <article class="page-container">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1 class="page-title">About FreeFileTools</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle">Free, open-source, client-side web utility tools engineered for privacy and speed.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="page-body">
      <section>
        <h2>Our Mission</h2>
        <p>
          FreeFileTools was created with a fundamental mission: web file processing utilities should be completely free, lightning fast, and 100% private.
        </p>
        <p>
          Unlike traditional web file converters that upload your sensitive documents, graphics, and photographs to remote cloud servers, FreeFileTools operates <strong>entirely inside your web browser</strong>. Your files are processed locally in your device memory and never leave your system.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Client-Side Technology &amp; Privacy Architecture</h2>
        <p>
          We leverage modern browser standards to deliver serverless file conversion:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>HTML5 Canvas API:</strong> Native 2D context image re-encoding for high-performance format conversion (PNG, JPG, WebP, AVIF).</li>
          <li><strong>Magic Number Header Inspection:</strong> Binary byte verification to ensure file integrity directly in local RAM.</li>
          <li><strong>Vanilla JavaScript &amp; WebAssembly:</strong> Lightweight execution pipelines with zero third-party framework overhead.</li>
          <li><strong>JSZip Engine:</strong> Client-side ZIP archive compilation for multi-file batch downloads.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Why Zero-Server-Upload Privacy Matters</h2>
        <p>
          Uploading private photos, personal graphics, or business documents to cloud servers poses inherent privacy risks, including data breaches, accidental cloud exposure, and third-party data tracking. By processing files locally:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>100% Private:</strong> Your files never touch a remote server disk or database.</li>
          <li><strong>No Data Caps:</strong> Process unlimited batch files without artificial file size or daily upload quotas.</li>
          <li><strong>Instant Speed:</strong> Conversions execute at your device's memory bus speed without network upload latency.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact &amp; Support</h2>
        <p>
          Have questions, technical inquiries, or feature suggestions? Reach out to our dedicated support team at <a href="mailto:sajeepriyangika81@gmail.com">sajeepriyangika81@gmail.com</a> or visit our <a href="/contact">Contact Page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-container {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-16);
  }

  .page-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .page-title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-3xl);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .page-subtitle {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .page-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .page-body h2 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .page-body p {
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-loose);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .page-body ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-loose);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .page-body a {
    color: var(--color-brand-400);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .page-body a:hover {
    color: var(--color-brand-300);
  }
</style>
